split: central: Retry scanning when it fails to start

start_scanning() sets is_scanning before calling bt_le_scan_start() and
leaves it set when that fails. Every later call then returns early
("already running"), so the central never scans again and a disconnected
peripheral is not found until reboot.

bt_le_scan_start() can fail transiently: with -EPERM while another
connection is being initiated on controllers that can't scan and
initiate at the same time (e.g. an app connecting to another BLE device
as central when the peripheral drops).

Clear is_scanning on failure and retry after a second.

--- a/app/src/split/bluetooth/central.c
+++ b/app/src/split/bluetooth/central.c
@@ -882,6 +882,10 @@
     }
 }
 
+static void start_scanning_retry_fn(struct k_work *work) { start_scanning(); }
+
+static K_WORK_DELAYABLE_DEFINE(start_scanning_retry, start_scanning_retry_fn);
+
 static int start_scanning(void) {
     if (!is_enabled) {
         LOG_DBG("Not scanning, we're disabled");
@@ -912,6 +916,11 @@
     int err = bt_le_scan_start(BT_LE_SCAN_PASSIVE, split_central_device_found);
     if (err < 0) {
         LOG_ERR("Scanning failed to start (err %d)", err);
+        // Don't claim to be scanning: that would make every later call return early and the
+        // peripheral would never be found again. The start can fail transiently, e.g. with
+        // -EPERM while another connection is being initiated, so try again shortly.
+        is_scanning = false;
+        k_work_reschedule(&start_scanning_retry, K_SECONDS(1));
         return err;
     }
 
